  "title": "Erdős Problem #917",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $k\\geq 4$ and $f_k(n)$ be the largest number of edges in a graph on $n$ vertices which has chromatic number $k$ and is critical (i.e. deleting any edge reduces the chromatic number).\nIs it true that $ f_k(n) \\gg_k n^2? $ Is it true that $ f_6(n)\\sim n^2/4? $ More generally, is it true that, for $k\\geq 6$, $ f_k(n) \\sim \\frac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\frac{1}{\\lfloor k/3\\rfloor}\\right)n^2? $ ",
